<article class="env-lemma" id="0H97">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H97">Lemma <span data-tag="0H97">17.17.4</span>.</a> Let $f : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. If $\mathcal{G}$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-module, then $f^*\mathcal{G}$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemma <a href="/tag/05NE" data-tag="05NE">17.17.2</a> with Sheaves, Lemma <a href="/tag/0098" data-tag="0098">6.26.4</a> and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HI" data-tag="00HI">10.39.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>